.TH SYNC_FILE_RANGE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
sync_file_range \- Linux x86-64 syscall 277
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_260_299.h>
.B int sync_file_range(int descriptor, off_t offset, off_t length, unsigned int flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Synchronizes part of a file using Linux sync_file_range.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sync_file_range (2)
